> 501ivan file in it; does anyone know how I get to play with it again?

Not sure exactly what the problem might be, but possible fixes that 
spring to mind:

Save your new game, compare permissions, fix those on /save/501ivan 
to match.

If your /save/501ivan doesn't have a .Z or .gz extension then 
compress or gzip (respectively) it.

Any files with 'lock' in the name in nethackdir? delete (or rename) 
them.
 
> Is the 501 at the start of the filename significant, in that my user
> name is ivan, not 501ivan? Do I need to replace the 501 with another
> number?

The 501 is your unix user ID, it should be there. [if you look in 
your logfile or record file you'll see the 501 embedded in each 
line - unless someone else also plays, in which case you'll see 502 
etc as well.]

